            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0583" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857.014/41</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Swenson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1927-06-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received
                        July 6.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1015</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatch No. 703, of
                    December 7, 1925,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d509-f1"/> regarding the alleged rights
                    of Mr. Christopher Evensen Ruud on <pb facs="0584" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/> the
                    Island of Jan Mayen, I have the honor to report that the Storting has just
                    passed a bill appropriating the sum of ten thousand kroner to Mr. Ruud as an
                    equitable settlement in connection with his occupation of the Island in 1917.
                    The appropriation is conditional on Mr. Ruud and his creditors assigning
                    whatever rights they may have on Jan Mayen to the Norwegian Government, and the
                    Department of Finance is authorized to negotiate with the interested parties and
                    to make payment upon reaching an agreement.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurits S.
                    Swenson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
